            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="57aded3d-4d3f-3d65-b03a-7392ab36aef2">electronics</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="6086e8b4-40cc-356e-837f-debbd03b1a27">component</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The data represent a typical small electrolyt-capacitor (hight &lt; 2 cm), used in the information and communication technology. Material data are taken from datasheets of producers of such capacitors and from the literature. Infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents 1 kg of capacitor with a weight of 1.29 gram/unit. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated, which are explained in separate modules. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: 7b1aff74-0f04-3fe3-9ede-8b410a1d8299</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
        <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
            <referenceToReferenceFlow>1</referenceToReferenceFlow>
        </quantitativeReference>
        <time xmlns:olca="http://openlca.org/ilcd-extensions" olca:startDate="1672527600000" olca:endDate="1890774000000">
